<author id="708738">LanX</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">good try :) But ...&lt;P&gt;


&lt;c&gt;
  DB&lt;262&gt; sub mysay (;+@) { print @_ }

  DB&lt;263&gt; mysay 1,2,3
123
  DB&lt;264&gt; mysay 1..3

  DB&lt;265&gt; mysay 1..3,4..6
456
  DB&lt;268&gt;&lt;/c&gt;&lt;P&gt;

It's enforcing scalar context on the first argument, and this is one of the unfortunate cases where an operator is changing it's meaning on context. :(&lt;P&gt;

